# What Docker must NOT send to the daemon as build context.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS (#61). docker/docker-compose.yml's haf-stats-rewriter declares
# `build: context: ..` -- the REPO ROOT -- because Dockerfile.rewriter COPYs from both
# endpoints/ and docker/. That build is not hypothetical: CI publishes only SHA tags, so
# the default `:latest` does not resolve and Compose falls back to building it, which is
# the behaviour the README documents.
#
# .gitignore does NOT restrict a build context; only this file does. Without it the
# context tars up docker/blockchain/ -- the pre-synced HAF block_log the README's own
# Prerequisites tell the operator to put there, which is multiple GB -- on every build.
#
# Keep endpoints/ and docker/ OUT of the exclusions: Dockerfile.rewriter COPYs
# docker/haf_stats_nginx.conf.template, docker/rewriter_entrypoint.sh and
# endpoints/rewrite_rules.conf, and the main Dockerfile COPYs db/, endpoints/ and
# scripts/. Excluding a COPY source fails the build loudly, which is the good case --
# but it fails it.

# Chain data and runtime state. The big one.
docker/blockchain/
docker/blockchain
**/datadir/
**/shm_dir/
*.log

# Version control and CI metadata
.git/
.gitignore
.gitlab-ci.yml
.gitattributes

# Local environment overrides
docker/.env.local

# Python caches and the venv scripts/openapi_rewrite.sh builds
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.openapi_venv/
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/

# Documentation and tests: neither Dockerfile COPYs these.
docs/
tests/
README.md
CHANGELOG.md

# Extracted by install-test; never part of an image. (#78)
.baseline/
